# Copy to a project as `.envrc` (requires: eval "$(hearth-vault direnv-init)"
# in ~/.config/direnv/direnvrc).
#
# This exports HEARTH_VAULT_PREFIX -- a NAME, not a secret -- so that inside
# this directory `hearth-vault exec -- <cmd>` needs no --prefix.
#
# It deliberately does NOT load your secrets into the shell. If you are
# tempted to add `export API_KEY=$(hearth-vault export-env ...)` below: that
# is the exact pattern this tool exists to end. Every process launched from
# that shell inherits it, including every coding agent, and it will show up
# in the next `env` dump someone pastes into a bug report.
use hearth_vault

# If there is no .hearth-vault marker, name the prefix explicitly instead:
# use hearth_vault myapp/
